p.src:
A cautious capacity shorthand is $C_{\mathrm{scaled}}
\sim
C_{\mathrm{owner}}
+
\sum_{i=1}^{n} C_{\mathrm{operator},i},$ where $C_{\mathrm{operator},i}$ is the reliable capacity of the $i$-th trained operator. The symbol $\sim$ matters. This is not a financial formula from the interview. It is a note-writing reconstruction of AK’s mechanism: capacity increases when trained people can carry repeatable work under procedures and supervision.

