p.src:
The learning update after a difficult attempt is: $\mathrm{Skill}_{t+1}
=
\mathrm{Skill}_{t}
+
\Delta(\mathrm{attempt},\mathrm{loss},\mathrm{correction}).$ This is a standard reconstruction of his spoken claim: sometimes one loses, sometimes one wins, but without trying one never learns the skill set needed to keep growing.

