A compact way to write the rule is $\mathrm{Growth}
\propto
\mathrm{Accountability}
\times
\mathrm{Correction}.$ If accountability is zero, correction rarely begins. This is why AK says that if one always thinks everybody else did everything wrong, one never gets better.

